### =====================================================================
### mcp-server-service: the MCP tools of the AI assistant, called by hand
###
### MCP is JSON-RPC over HTTP: every request is a POST to /mcp with "method" and "params".
### Normally only mcp-client-service calls this (the model decides which tool); these requests show what it gets.
### Needs the API gateway and the catalog services running (the tools read live data through the gateway).
### Run them in VS Code (REST Client extension) or IntelliJ IDEA.
### =====================================================================

@mcp = http://localhost:8115
# The local default (application-local.yml). Never use it outside your machine.
@apiKey = local-dev-mcp-api-key-0123456789abcdef

### 1. Without the API key -> 401 {"success":false,"message":"A valid X-MCP-API-Key header is required", ...}
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list", "params": {}}

### 2. Start: the server introduces itself (name grocery-tools, its instructions, "tools" capability)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "initialize",
 "params": {"protocolVersion": "2025-11-25", "capabilities": {}, "clientInfo": {"name": "http-file", "version": "1.0"}}}

### 3. The 7 tools with their descriptions and parameter schemas (what the model sees)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "tools/list", "params": {}}

### 4. searchProducts: "amul butter" -> OK, prices as "₹56", stock "Only 3 left", store "Fresh Mart"
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "searchProducts", "arguments": {"query": "amul butter"}}}

### 5. searchProducts: something the shop does not sell -> NOT_FOUND (the assistant must say so, never guess)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "searchProducts", "arguments": {"query": "iphone 15"}}}

### 6. searchProducts: a category by a loose name ("fruit" -> Fruits), up to ₹100, only in stock
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "method": "tools/call",
 "params": {"name": "searchProducts", "arguments": {"category": "fruit", "maxPrice": 100, "inStockOnly": true}}}

### 7. searchProducts without arguments -> INVALID_INPUT with a hint how to call it
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "searchProducts", "arguments": {}}}

### 8. getProductDetails by name (the best search match), as the model does in a follow-up ("is it in stock?")
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getProductDetails", "arguments": {"product": "amul butter"}}}

### 9. getProductReviews by productId (from a searchProducts result): the rating and the 3 newest reviews
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getProductReviews", "arguments": {"product": "1"}}}

### 10. listCategories
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "listCategories", "arguments": {}}}

### 11. listCurrentOffers: every coupon once, with "All stores" / "Only at Fresh Mart"
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "listCurrentOffers", "arguments": {}}}

### 12. listCurrentOffers of one store (a part of the name is enough)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "listCurrentOffers", "arguments": {"storeName": "green basket"}}}

### 13. getDeliveryRules: fee, free delivery from, minimum order, plus a summary sentence
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 13, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getDeliveryRules", "arguments": {}}}

### 14. listStores: address, phone, "Open now", opening hours grouped by day
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "listStores", "arguments": {}}}

### 15. Customer tools: log in as customer1 (seed data) through the gateway ...
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "customer1@grocery.com", "password": "Password@123"}

### 16. ... getMyOrders with the customer's token in X-User-Token (mcp-client-service sends it for every logged-in user)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Token: {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getMyOrders", "arguments": {}}}

### 17. getMyCart with the token
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Token: {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getMyCart", "arguments": {}}}

### 18. getMyOrders WITHOUT a token -> LOGIN_REQUIRED
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 18, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getMyOrders", "arguments": {}}}

### 19. Panel tools: log in as vendor1 (seed data) through the gateway ...
# @name vendorLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "vendor1@grocery.com", "password": "Password@123"}

### 20. ... getVendorStoreToday with the vendor's token
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Token: {{vendorLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 20, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getVendorStoreToday", "arguments": {}}}

### 21. getVendorOrders of one status ("new" = waiting for the store to accept)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Token: {{vendorLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 21, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getVendorOrders", "arguments": {"status": "new"}}}

### 22. Log in as admin (seed data) ...
# @name adminLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@grocery.com", "password": "Password@123"}

### 23. ... getAdminWaitingWork with the admin's token
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Token: {{adminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 23, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getAdminWaitingWork", "arguments": {}}}

### 24. The admin tool with the vendor's token -> LOGIN_REQUIRED (the gateway answers 403)
POST {{mcp}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-MCP-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Token: {{vendorLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 24, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "getAdminOverview", "arguments": {}}}

### 25. Health (no API key needed): used by Kubernetes
GET {{mcp}}/actuator/health
